<title>UK: London tea auction sees good general demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees good general demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Monday's London tea auction saw good general demand with offshore teas often closing at firmer rates, the official report said.</p>
<p>Quality Assams fetched a high of 200 pence for the best types with the rest tending easier.</p>
<p>Prices for Bright East Africans increased by up to five pence per kg with medium types fully firm to dearer.</p>
<p>Offshore teas met with good demand at firmer rates.</p>
<p>-London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8071</p>
